1
00:01:09,761 --> 00:01:12,304
Thank you, captain.

2
00:01:18,728 --> 00:01:19,728
Well?

3
00:01:19,896 --> 00:01:22,147
The target is still in the same place.

4
00:01:28,571 --> 00:01:30,906
Target is leaving the apartment.
Ten seconds.

5
00:01:31,074 --> 00:01:32,324
Start the engine.

6
00:02:00,103 --> 00:02:01,937
Underwear or no underwear today?

7
00:02:03,481 --> 00:02:05,816
Be a little more professional, guys.

8
00:02:13,032 --> 00:02:16,410
She's turning left.
She's going to her usual café.

9
00:02:29,424 --> 00:02:30,590
May I take your order?

10
00:02:30,758 --> 00:02:32,718
A tea with milk,
an orange juice and...

11
00:02:32,885 --> 00:02:34,136
And a croissant.

12
00:02:34,303 --> 00:02:36,012
It's already ordered.

13
00:02:36,180 --> 00:02:37,305
Thank you.

14
00:02:44,147 --> 00:02:45,272
Do you have a visual?

15
00:02:45,815 --> 00:02:47,983
We have a visual.
She's drinking her tea.

16
00:02:48,484 --> 00:02:49,651
Come again?

17
00:02:49,819 --> 00:02:51,403
She's drinking her tea!

18
00:02:51,779 --> 00:02:53,655
Did you ask for a tea, sir?

19
00:02:53,823 --> 00:02:55,490
No, no. Thank you.

20
00:03:11,549 --> 00:03:13,467
I'm looking for Ms. Elise Ward.

21
00:03:13,634 --> 00:03:15,677
That's Ms. Ward over there.

22
00:03:20,850 --> 00:03:21,850
Elise Ward?

23
00:03:22,018 --> 00:03:23,894
- Yes, it's me.
- I have an envelope for you.

24
00:03:24,061 --> 00:03:27,731
Somebody is talking to her.
Looks like a courier.

25
00:04:06,395 --> 00:04:08,104
No, no. It's okay. It's a gift.

26
00:04:14,946 --> 00:04:16,404
Goodbye.

27
00:04:27,041 --> 00:04:29,417
- Take him.
- Let's get him.

28
00:04:31,963 --> 00:04:34,881
Sir, stop! Police!

29
00:04:36,926 --> 00:04:39,094
What's going on?

30
00:04:39,470 --> 00:04:41,930
- You are under arrest.
- Financial Crimes Division.

31
00:04:42,098 --> 00:04:43,640
Division what?

32
00:04:44,141 --> 00:04:45,267
Guys, I'm working!

33
00:05:56,213 --> 00:05:58,340
Daniel, get over there now.

34
00:06:50,351 --> 00:06:52,727
Drive around to the other side! Go!

35
00:07:03,906 --> 00:07:05,365
Turn right at the end.

36
00:07:07,076 --> 00:07:08,535
Faster!

37
00:16:47,739 --> 00:16:49,824
How about a photo?

38
00:16:50,075 --> 00:16:51,534
Go right ahead.

39
00:16:53,036 --> 00:16:54,453
Make me look good.

40
00:19:15,554 --> 00:19:16,595
Memorize his face.

41
00:19:17,639 --> 00:19:19,724
The train arrives in ten minutes.

42
00:19:19,891 --> 00:19:22,143
As soon as he steps off, arrest him.

43
00:22:31,499 --> 00:22:33,250
Understood.

44
00:22:38,423 --> 00:22:39,965
The operation has been cancelled.

45
00:22:40,175 --> 00:22:42,468
Return to headquarters. Quickly.

46
00:22:43,011 --> 00:22:44,470
On the other side.

47
00:26:22,897 --> 00:26:24,523
Welcome to Venezia, signora.

48
00:41:26,800 --> 00:41:29,844
- He doesn't look like Pearce.
- Boss said he might not.

49
00:41:30,012 --> 00:41:31,304
Grab him!

50
00:42:28,612 --> 00:42:30,071
Boss wants him alive, you idiot!

51
00:42:40,624 --> 00:42:42,166
She's coming back.

52
00:43:04,523 --> 00:43:05,606
Prepare to intervene.

53
00:44:47,751 --> 00:44:49,168
Headquarters!

54
00:44:49,336 --> 00:44:51,212
Send me backup to the fruit market.

55
00:44:51,505 --> 00:44:53,673
I have a nutcase who wants to jump.

56
00:44:53,924 --> 00:44:55,132
Probably American.

57
00:44:59,346 --> 00:45:00,846
Stop, stop! Please!

58
00:45:05,686 --> 00:45:07,144
Don't do it!

59
00:45:21,910 --> 00:45:23,703
Bastard!

60
00:51:48,545 --> 00:51:52,089
Remember, don't shoot him!

61
00:55:56,084 --> 00:55:57,126
They are back.

62
00:55:59,504 --> 00:56:00,671
I come back tomorrow?

63
01:22:09,990 --> 01:22:11,824
I don't think she actually knows.

64
01:23:44,376 --> 01:23:46,043
No. Knife.

65
01:23:53,593 --> 01:23:55,135
This guy is crazy.

66
01:27:09,789 --> 01:27:10,998
This was the man on the boat.
